# Release automation writes to CHANGELOG.md on both main (stable) and staging
# (rc prereleases), so the two branches always have competing additions at the
# top of the file. `union` keeps both sides instead of raising a conflict on
# every staging -> main merge and every back-merge.
#
# Entries can land interleaved after a merge; the next release regenerates the
# section headings, so it self-corrects.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union

# package-lock.json is generated. Never hand-resolve it: take either side and
# run `npm install` to regenerate.
package-lock.json -diff
